        "ledgerRule": "the predecessor's ledger is the steps' attested records carried in the securelock's signed output envelopes (RESERVATION-DESIGN.md §2); the securelock stopped by transfer writes no result envelope, so fields 4-6, 12 and 14 are signed over those records, the ones landed by toBlock (here the ESR example's three commits, all landed)",
        "codeRule": "SERVICE_TRANSFER_FORCED (42) is asserted by the trustedzone alone when the securelock is still busy HANDOVER_FORCE_SECONDS (two minutes) before the toBlock of the order's window, its end window or an announced one (RESERVATION-DESIGN.md §2, §3): the securelock is sent the signed transfer control and stops the step in hand, discarding the step's held commit authorisations, the commits signed by then are landed, and the result is signed over the steps' attested records (fields 4-6, 12 and 14 non-zero here, the ESR example's three commits) with the session status transfer-forced (07), the code taken from the outputs the trustedzone holds once the securelock's heartbeat has stopped (every forwarded input answered: 41). Not a securelock code and not a refund code: validated as SERVICE_TRANSFERRED is, the session gate admitting unanswered input rows as the tail of the inputs only, at least one (here the second). The unanswered inputs (every etny-si row of the predecessor's request without an etny-so row acknowledging it, signed by the predecessor's task wallet, landed by the predecessor's bound, its result's block inside the window and toBlock otherwise, the rows' blocks from the PoX's OutputRowAdded logs, in sequence order) are replayed by the successor as its first inputs, on the state the last commit left; the runner resends nothing (the replayed example)."
